{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774977279,"nonce":"iehZzCVdzde1pWNj0PkE0TOonZU=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM75M7oA","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/35","origin":"github"},"title":"Discuss: when to clear stale mission on GUIDED mode entry","message":"## Summary\n\nWhen echo_helm transitions from standby to active, it arms the FCU in GUIDED mode.\nIf ArduPilot has a stale mission loaded, it immediately begins navigating to the\nfirst waypoint — even though no cmd_vel has been sent.\n\n## Observed Behavior\n\nDuring testing (#31), arming in GUIDED caused props to spin up gradually with\nsteering input. The FCU was trying to reach a waypoint ~12m from the current\nGPS position. No cmd_vel had been published.\n\nRoot cause: `MIS_TOTAL=2` — two waypoints were loaded in the FCU from a previous\nsession. GUIDED mode picked up the first one.\n\n## Questions to Discuss\n\n- Should the mission be cleared every time the system enters GUIDED?\n- Or once at startup (e.g., in core_launch or echo_helm activation)?\n- Should echo_helm send a zero-velocity setpoint immediately after arming in GUIDED\n  as a safety measure, regardless of mission state?\n- Does this affect IzzyBoat as well, or only BizzyBoat?\n\n## Context\n\n- BizzyBoat has throttle + steering servo (not differential drive)\n- echo_helm `rc_mode=False` — uses GUIDED + cmd_vel setpoints\n- ArduRover V4.5.7 on CubeOrange\n\nPart of #31\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.6`","files":null}]}